syntax:
Access specifiers within class or struct definitions:

class ClassName {
public:
    typedef int PublicType;
private:
    typedef int PrivateType;
};

Accessing nested types:

ClassName::PublicType var1; // OK
ClassName::PrivateType var2; // Error if accessed outside the class

code_example:
namespace A {
    class BB {
    public:
        // public members
    };
    class B {
    private:
        // private members
    };
}
void f() {
    A::BB x; // OK, BB is public, accessible outside namespace
    A::B y; // Error, B is private, inaccessible outside namespace
}
